<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s248S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s248p26">In reply</span> we will first <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w2">set forth</span> a relevant <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w1">passage</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s248p27">and</span> then we will <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w4">explicate</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w3">passage</span>. Here is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w5">first</span>. The text called The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w6">Abbreviation of the Greater Way</span> says, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s248p18">Insofar as</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w7">craving spirits</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w8">animals</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w9">Humans</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s248p10">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w11">pleasure beings</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s248w12">each according To their class</span>, have <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w17">differing</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w15">perceptions</span> Of a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w14">single</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w13">thing</span>, we <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w20">say</span> it <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s248w19">has no reality</span>. <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w25">Asvabhava</span>, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w24">venered</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w23">layman with lifetime vows</span>, has <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s248w22">explained</span> the passage. His words include the following:<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s248p21"><span class="nul">The predicative yin in &#x27;dod pa yin is fused into the finite assertion say; no separate copular English word is present. Its grammatical contribution is retained by that predication.</span></span></span>
